* Behavioural op-amp models: single dominant pole at the gain-bandwidth product,
* output limited to the rails, 1 MOhm differential input, 10 Ohm output.
* These are what the front-end design depends on (gain, bandwidth, swing),
* not what a vendor model adds (noise, distortion, slew).  Vendor models for
* the OPA1612, THS4521 and OPA2810 exist on ti.com and can be dropped in here.
*
* OPA1612: 40 MHz GBW, 100 dB Aol
.subckt OPA1612 inp inn vcc vee out
Rin inp inn 1e6
Ein 1 0 inp inn 1
R1 1 2 1k
C1 2 0 {1/(2*3.14159*1k*40e6/1e5)}
Eol 3 0 2 0 1e5
Blim 4 0 V = max(min(V(3), V(vcc)-1.2), V(vee)+1.2)
Rout 4 out 10
.ends
* THS4521: fully differential, 145 MHz GBW, VOCM input, 3.3 V single supply
.subckt THS4521 inp inn vocm vcc vee outn outp
Rin inp inn 1e6
Ein 1 0 inp inn 1
R1 1 2 1k
C1 2 0 {1/(2*3.14159*1k*145e6/1e4)}
Eol 3 0 2 0 1e4
* differential output about vocm; each side limited to the rails
Bop 5 0 V = max(min(V(vocm) + V(3)/2, V(vcc)-0.2), V(vee)+0.2)
Bon 6 0 V = max(min(V(vocm) - V(3)/2, V(vcc)-0.2), V(vee)+0.2)
Routp 5 outp 10
Routn 6 outn 10
.ends
* OPA2810: 105 MHz GBW, 100 dB
.subckt OPA2810 inp inn vcc vee out
Rin inp inn 1e6
Ein 1 0 inp inn 1
R1 1 2 1k
C1 2 0 {1/(2*3.14159*1k*105e6/1e5)}
Eol 3 0 2 0 1e5
Blim 4 0 V = max(min(V(3), V(vcc)-0.5), V(vee)+0.5)
Rout 4 out 10
.ends
